{"h":3406,"lines":[{"x":0.86977705096572988,"h":0.017070354746148264,"c":1,"y":0.045717531136552081,"w":0.089475409189859967,"t":"Reading"},{"y":0.095930232605573651,"c":1,"x":0.061855666984286302,"t":"READING PASSAGE 3","h":0.01453488361674482,"w":0.32783505757649739},{"x":0.06185565164526878,"t":"You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 27-40, which are based on Reading","y":0.13358778627046375,"w":0.88247426350911451,"h":0.017615971814445075,"c":1},{"h":0.015988371754420694,"t":"Passage 3 below.","y":0.15261627922574506,"w":0.17938144683837892,"c":1,"x":0.061855668183903326},{"t":"Reducing the Effects of Climate Change","w":0.50721649169921879,"h":0.022019964768056344,"c":1,"x":0.25154639326882555,"y":0.19318849078564559},{"c":1,"w":0.78144327799479163,"t":"Mark Rowe reports on the increasingly ambitious geo-engineering projects","x":0.11546392953353206,"y":0.23253082830325877,"h":0.021829636462352253},{"h":0.020551967116852699,"x":0.36494844780168362,"y":0.25425719328026841,"t":"being explored by scientists","w":0.28247423807779953,"c":1},{"y":0.28625954196935266,"x":0.098969068915434943,"w":0.78556701660156247,"h":0.017615971814445075,"t":"Such is our dependence on fossil fuels, and such is the volume of carbon dioxide already","c":1},{"y":0.30310194799712653,"w":0.81456960042317694,"c":1,"h":0.021014844678250433,"t":"released into the atmosphere, that many experts agree that significant global warming is now","x":0.10509230378034327},{"c":1,"x":0.10309279818128829,"h":0.017450394801231228,"y":0.32266588380760775,"t":"inevitable. They believe that the best we can do is keep it at a reasonable level, and at present","w":0.81855667114257802},{"h":0.017615971814445075,"w":0.83711339314778632,"x":0.10515464352735393,"y":0.34145625360264775,"c":1,"t":"the only serious option for doing this is cutting back on our carbon emissions. But while a few"},{"w":0.8206185404459635,"h":0.01889534914976565,"c":1,"t":"countries are making major strides in this regard, the majority are having great difficulty even","x":0.10721650312753374,"y":0.35901162751450677},{"t":"stemming the rate of increase, let alone reversing it. Consequently, an increasing number of","x":0.10515463737602848,"y":0.37786259572671221,"c":1,"h":0.019083969465648831,"w":0.8082474263509114},{"x":0.10515464053930752,"w":0.82268040974934886,"h":0.018934609395787061,"c":1,"t":"scientists are beginning to explore the alternative of geo-engineering - a term which generally","y":0.39680232541035521},{"h":0.015988371754420583,"c":1,"x":0.10515462963373873,"t":"refers to the intentional large-scale manipulation of the environment. According to its","y":0.41715116295772148,"w":0.75670104980468755},{"x":0.10515463367352566,"y":0.43452730456832489,"w":0.82474227905273434,"h":0.017615971814445186,"t":"proponents, geo-engineering is the equivalent of a backup generator: if Plan A - reducing our","c":1},{"h":0.017445274751744844,"y":0.45348837181725954,"w":0.83092783610026033,"c":1,"x":0.10515463854296286,"t":"dependency on fossil fuels - fails, we require a Plan B, employing grand schemes to slow down"},{"y":0.46835153323726209,"h":0.023227304132700022,"w":0.36146339416503903,"c":1,"t":"or reverse the process of global warming.","x":0.10489873824885426},{"t":"Geo-engineering has been shown to work, at least on a small localised scale. For decades, May","h":0.017441859892096456,"c":1,"x":0.10515465262107559,"y":0.50000000027093683,"w":0.82680409749348971},{"t":"Day parades in Moscow have taken place under clear blue skies, aircraft having deposited dry","y":0.51879036990628014,"c":1,"x":0.10515464723430587,"w":0.8206185404459635,"h":0.017615971814445186},{"x":0.10309279059459556,"w":0.81443298339843762,"y":0.53633720890985548,"h":0.01889534914976565,"c":1,"t":"ice, silver iodide and cement powder to disperse clouds. Many of the schemes now suggested"},{"t":"look to do the opposite, and reduce the amount of sunlight reaching the planet. The most","c":1,"x":0.10309277817979932,"h":0.017615971814445075,"y":0.55519671191152808,"w":0.79381444295247394},{"y":0.5739870815399114,"t":"eye-catching idea of all is suggested by Professor Roger Angel of the University of Arizona. His","x":0.1051546385626682,"w":0.83092783610026044,"c":1,"h":0.017615971814445075},{"w":0.81649485270182287,"t":"scheme would employ up to 16 trillion minute spacecraft, each weighing about one gram, to","h":0.017441861012089777,"c":1,"x":0.10309277972463861,"y":0.59302325553721269},{"c":1,"t":"form a transparent, sunlight-refracting sunshade in an orbit 1.5 million km above the Earth.","w":0.81460652669270828,"y":0.60968690484885091,"x":0.10300034747945706,"h":0.021023979343810839},{"y":0.62798784939750851,"t":"This could, argues Angel, reduce the amount of light reaching the Earth by two per cent.","x":0.10300872381752336,"h":0.021068649157592989,"w":0.78162470499674486,"c":1},{"y":0.6584302323992659,"w":0.8144329833984375,"t":"The majority of geo-engineering projects so far carried out - which include planting forests","h":0.018903883498903484,"c":1,"x":0.090721652523336999},{"w":0.82474227905273445,"t":"in deserts and depositing iron in the ocean to stimulate the growth of algae - have focused on","c":1,"h":0.017441861012089666,"x":0.1010309222262101,"y":0.67732558111951779},{"h":0.017615971814445075,"t":"achieving a general cooling of the Earth. But some look specifically at reversing the melting","w":0.80206186930338541,"c":1,"y":0.69612448621148182,"x":0.10309277658486185},{"t":"at the poles, particularly the Arctic. The reasoning is that if you replenish the ice sheets and","x":0.10309278358119466,"y":0.71366279041800251,"h":0.017441861012089777,"c":1,"w":0.80000000000000004},{"t":"frozen waters of the high latitudes, more light will be reflected back into space, so reducing the","y":0.73253082822175952,"c":1,"x":0.1010309389942744,"w":0.83505152384440118,"h":0.017469172049324744},{"h":0.017615971814445075,"w":0.35463918050130205,"y":0.75132119784020068,"t":"warming of the oceans and atmosphere.","x":0.10103092511500619,"c":1},{"t":"The concept of releasing aerosol sprays into the stratosphere above the Arctic has been proposed","y":0.77906976751034718,"x":0.10309279238908819,"h":0.017465758309669566,"c":1,"w":0.84123708089192706},{"h":0.017441861012089777,"t":"by several scientists. This would involve using sulphur or hydrogen sulphide aerosols so that","x":0.10309278157308749,"y":0.79796511600179132,"w":0.8082474263509114,"c":1},{"w":0.83092783610026044,"c":1,"t":"sulphur dioxide would form clouds, which would, in turn, lead to a global dimming. The idea","y":0.8167938929972075,"x":0.10103092721008257,"h":0.017615971814445075},{"x":0.10309277604382525,"y":0.83430232530504922,"w":0.83298970540364581,"h":0.017441861012089777,"c":1,"t":"is modelled on historic volcanic explosions, such as that of Mount Pinatubo in the Philippines"},{"t":"in 1991, which led to a short-term cooling of global temperatures by 0.5 °C. Scientists have","x":0.10096019468049613,"c":1,"h":0.021001561557413617,"y":0.85130144392258356,"w":0.81044138590494796},{"w":0.80000000000000004,"h":0.017615971814445075,"c":1,"x":0.10103092775081715,"y":0.87199060463004896,"t":"also scrutinised whether it's possible to preserve the ice sheets of Greenland with reinforced"},{"y":0.8899221881116498,"t":"high-tension cables, preventing icebergs from moving into the sea. Meanwhile in the Russian","h":0.019961394636475616,"x":0.10096785657736111,"c":1,"w":0.82074712117513016},{"x":0.10103093146152142,"y":0.90986494396410666,"w":0.78350514729817711,"h":0.017460637700186687,"c":1,"t":"Arctic, geo-engineering plans include the planting of millions of birch trees. Whereas the"},{"c":1,"x":0.10103093586565554,"w":0.82061854044596361,"t":"region's native evergreen pines shade the snow and absorb radiation, birches would shed their","y":0.9286553141491275,"h":0.017615971814445075},{"c":1,"t":"leltsresources.org","w":0.29146217346191411,"x":0.35219444028158703,"y":0.95433624955947682,"h":0.022583511809496359},{"c":1,"t":"25","h":0.01453488361674482,"w":0.026804122924804608,"x":0.91958762915615433,"y":0.95494186045114138}],"w":2400}